    "limits": "Bazel -c opt native Rust public API versus published default TypeScript public API on Node/V8. Same four inputs per workload, all per-input outputs checked before timing. Native run first, then TS; separate runtimes, no FFI/WASM. Native 256 warmup, nine alternating 16384-call samples against temporal_rs; TS 20000 warmup, nine 50000-call samples. Both consume outputs; strings use FNV-1a 32-bit, avoiding TS BigInt hashing. Rust black_box and integer sum; TS number sum with low-32-bit reduction for BigInt outputs. Parsed values and calendar registries initialized outside timing. Rust calendar fields are one aggregate; TS reads three getters. TS may cache fields. UTC/fixed-offset zoned parsing only; no named-zone, startup, Hermes binding or conformance speed claim. Native temporal_rs reference retained as separate comparison.",
